WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.150
Your AI already does a lot of your work.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:04.810
Why stop there?

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.470
How much more could it carry?

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.070
That's the first of four questions: coverage.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.230
How much of your recurring work is actually set up in context, projects, agents and skills?

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.570
Then friction: what still needs correcting?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.270
And cost: what takes more time and tokens than it should?

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.950
And the fourth is a retrospective with your system itself.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.910
You bring real examples,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.750
and it finds which of its own files causes each friction.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.490
It's like a sports team after a match: they watch the replay together,

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.480
keep what worked, and play the next game better.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:47.440
So in this adventure, you move more work into your system, and fix each friction in the file behind it.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.500
Then the retrospective becomes a routine:

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.020
a skill that offers the next review on its own.
